{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Falsifying the `confirm_store is None` hypothesis (AC4, empirically)\n\nA parallel reading of the code suggested the flake might be the test intermittently taking\nthe storeless path, making the missing summary CORRECT and pointing at a production\nunder-count. That is ruled out, and the evidence is in this module already.\n\n**The per-item line only exists on the storeful path.** In `_inbound_unlink_one`\n(`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound_records.py:575-585`) the\n\"declining the inbound removal of ...\" WARNING is emitted inside\n`if confirm_store is not None and not confirm_store.is_confirmed(...)`. Its presence in the\nfailing capture is therefore positive proof that `confirm_store` was NOT None in the failing\nrun. The two candidate mechanisms are mutually exclusive and the log itself discriminates\nbetween them.\n\n**And a storeless pass produces no decline at all.** With no store the guard is bypassed and\nthe removal is APPLIED. That is already pinned by the sibling test in this very module,\n`test_unopenable_store_declines_nothing`, which patches `_open_peer_confirmation_store` to\nreturn `None` and asserts `applied == 1` and the link is gone. So the storeless path emits\nNEITHER line — not the per-item one and not the summary — which is not the observed failure\nshape.\n\n**So `declined == 0` when the store is None is truthful, not an under-report:** nothing was\ndeclined, because the removal went through. There is no production defect here and no\nproduction logging behaviour is changed by this fix.\n\nFinal confirmation is behavioural, not argumentative: the fix touches only the test-side\nlogger-level containment and turns the deterministic reproduction from RED (1 failed, 15\npassed) to GREEN (16 passed). If the mechanism had been storeless-path selection, a change to\n`tests/_log_integrity.py` could not have altered the outcome."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786612842585941001,"uuid":"f9d2b6cc-e900-47b2-9175-38bd02d04b55"}